✅ Java Reserved Words – Short Notes (Updated)
🔹 1. Flow Control Statements

if / else – Conditional branching

switch – Multi-way selection (supports expressions since Java 14)

case – Defines switch branch

default – Executes if no case matches

for – Loop with init–condition–update

while – Entry-controlled loop

do – Exit-controlled loop

break – Terminates loop or switch

continue – Skips current iteration

return – Sends value back from method

🔹 2. Data Types

byte – 1-byte integer

short – 2-byte integer

int – 4-byte integer (default)

long – 8-byte integer

float – 4-byte decimal

double – 8-byte decimal (default)

char – Single Unicode character

boolean – true / false

🔹 3. Source File / OOP Keywords

class – Blueprint of an object

interface – 100% abstraction (default & static methods allowed)

extends – Inherits class or interface

implements – Implements interface

package – Namespace for classes

import – Access classes from other packages

🔹 4. Object-Level Keywords

new – Creates object

this – Refers to current object

super – Refers to parent class object

instanceof – Checks object type at runtime

🔹 5. Method Keywords

void – Method returns nothing

return – Returns value from method

🔹 6. Exception Handling

try – Wraps risky code

catch – Handles exception

finally – Always executes

throw – Explicitly throws exception

throws – Declares exception responsibility

🔹 7. Modifiers
Access Modifiers

public – Accessible everywhere

private – Within same class

protected – Same package + subclass

default – Same package only

Non-Access Modifiers

abstract – Incomplete method/class

final – Cannot be overridden/changed

static – Belongs to class

synchronized – Thread-safe method/block

volatile – Visible across threads

transient – Excluded from serialization

native – Implemented using C/C++

strictfp – Consistent floating-point behavior

🔹 8. Java 5 Keywords

enum – Fixed set of constants

assert – Used for debugging checks

🔹 9. Unused Reserved Words

goto – Reserved, not used

const – Reserved, not used

🔹 10. Predefined Constants (Literals)

true – Boolean literal

false – Boolean literal

null – No object reference

⚠️ Not keywords

🚀 Modern Java (VERY IMPORTANT)
🔹 Java 9 – Module System

module – Defines module

requires – Dependency on module

exports – Exposes package

opens – Opens for reflection

uses – Uses service

provides – Provides service implementation

to / with – Module access control

transitive – Inherited dependency

🔹 Java 10

var – Local variable type inference
⚠️ Not a keyword (reserved type name)

🔹 Java 14

yield – Returns value from switch expression

🔹 Java 14+

record – Immutable data class with auto-generated methods
